0.5.0: WebAssembly target - polajuice in the browser

'make' still builds the native binary; 'make wasm' compiles the same
core (pipeline, stb codecs, EXIF orientation parser) to WebAssembly via
Emscripten, so browser and CLI render byte-identical pixels for the same
input, camera, film, strength and seed.

New: src/web/pj_web.c shim (camera enumeration, render over MEMFS paths,
linear-light box-average preview downscale), web/index.html frontend
(drag-and-drop, camera/film selectors mirroring the CLI's canonical-film
behavior, strength/seed, preview at 1400px + full-size download,
client-side only), scripts/build_web.sh, scripts/stage_web_films.sh
(canonical cubes + films.json manifest), docs/WEB.md (build, local serve,
GitHub Pages deployment), 'make serve'.

The shim is plain C17 and is tested natively in make check
(tests/test_web_shim.c): enumeration, film and scalar modes, preview
downscale, and error paths.
